  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2x-3}{5}-\\frac{3x+1}{10}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x-7}{10}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x-3}{5}-\\frac{3x+1}{10}&=\\frac{2(2x-3)-(3x+1)}{10}\\\\\\frac{2(2x-3)-(3x+1)}{10}&=\\frac{4x-6-3x-1}{10}\\\\\\frac{4x-6-3x-1}{10}&=\\frac{x-7}{10}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{1}{x-y}-\\frac{2}{y-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{x-y}$",
          "worked": "Use $y-x=-(x-y)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x-y}-\\frac{2}{y-x}&=\\frac{1}{x-y}+\\frac{2}{x-y}\\\\\\frac{1}{x-y}+\\frac{2}{x-y}&=\\frac{3}{x-y}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2}{x^2-4}+\\frac{1}{x-2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x+4}{(x+2)(x-2)}$",
          "worked": "Factor $x^2-4=(x+2)(x-2)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{x^2-4}+\\frac{1}{x-2}&=\\frac{2+(x+2)}{(x+2)(x-2)}\\\\\\frac{2+(x+2)}{(x+2)(x-2)}&=\\frac{x+4}{(x+2)(x-2)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x}{x-y}-\\frac{y}{x^2-y^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x^2+xy-y}{(x+y)(x-y)}$",
          "worked": "Factor $x^2-y^2=(x+y)(x-y)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{x-y}-\\frac{y}{x^2-y^2}&=\\frac{x(x+y)-y}{(x+y)(x-y)}\\\\\\frac{x(x+y)-y}{(x+y)(x-y)}&=\\frac{x^2+xy-y}{(x+y)(x-y)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{3}{x+1}-\\frac{3}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{6}{(x+1)(x-1)}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{x+1}-\\frac{3}{x-1}&=\\frac{3(x-1)-3(x+1)}{(x+1)(x-1)}\\\\\\frac{3(x-1)-3(x+1)}{(x+1)(x-1)}&=\\frac{3x-3-3x-3}{(x+1)(x-1)}\\\\\\frac{3x-3-3x-3}{(x+1)(x-1)}&=-\\frac{6}{(x+1)(x-1)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2}{x^2-4}-\\frac{3}{x^2+5x-14}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{8-x}{(x-2)(x+2)(x+7)}$\n\nFactor both denominators and use their least common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4&=(x-2)(x+2)\\\\x^2+5x-14&=(x-2)(x+7)\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the common denominator $(x-2)(x+2)(x+7)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{x^2-4}-\\frac{3}{x^2+5x-14}&=\\frac{2(x+7)-3(x+2)}{(x-2)(x+2)(x+7)}\\\\2(x+7)-3(x+2)&=2x+14-3x-6\\\\2x+14-3x-6&=8-x\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe simplified fraction is $\\frac{8-x}{(x-2)(x+2)(x+7)}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x-y-\\frac{x^2}{x+y}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{y^2}{x+y}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x-y-\\frac{x^2}{x+y}&=\\frac{(x-y)(x+y)-x^2}{x+y}\\\\\\frac{(x-y)(x+y)-x^2}{x+y}&=\\frac{x^2-y^2-x^2}{x+y}\\\\\\frac{x^2-y^2-x^2}{x+y}&=-\\frac{y^2}{x+y}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{4}{x^2-4}-\\frac{1}{x-2}+\\frac{5}{x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4}{x+2}$, with $x\\ne 2,-2$.",
          "worked": "Use the common denominator $(x-2)(x+2)$, with $x\\ne 2,-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4}{x^2-4}-\\frac{1}{x-2}+\\frac{5}{x+2}&=\\frac{4-(x+2)+5(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\4-(x+2)+5(x-2)&=4x-8\\\\4x-8&=4(x-2)\\\\\\frac{4(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+2)}&=\\frac{4}{x+2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{x}{(x+3)^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{(x+3)^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{x}{(x+3)^2}&=\\frac{(x+3)-x}{(x+3)^2}\\\\\\frac{(x+3)-x}{(x+3)^2}&=\\frac{3}{(x+3)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{1}{(x+1)^2}-\\frac{1}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{x}{(x+1)^2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{(x+1)^2}-\\frac{1}{x+1}&=\\frac{1-(x+1)}{(x+1)^2}\\\\\\frac{1-(x+1)}{(x+1)^2}&=-\\frac{x}{(x+1)^2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$(x^{-1}+y^{-1})^{-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{xy}{x+y}$, with $x\\ne 0$, $y\\ne 0$ and $x+y\\ne 0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^{-1}+y^{-1}&=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}&=\\frac{x+y}{xy}\\\\(x^{-1}+y^{-1})^{-1}&=\\left(\\frac{x+y}{xy}\\right)^{-1}\\\\\\left(\\frac{x+y}{xy}\\right)^{-1}&=\\frac{xy}{x+y}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $x\\ne 0$, $y\\ne 0$ and $x+y\\ne 0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q14-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$(x+y)^{-1}(x^{-1}+y^{-1})$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{xy}$, with $x\\ne 0$, $y\\ne 0$ and $x+y\\ne 0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^{-1}+y^{-1}&=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}\\\\\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}&=\\frac{x+y}{xy}\\\\(x+y)^{-1}(x^{-1}+y^{-1})&=\\frac{1}{x+y}\\cdot\\frac{x+y}{xy}\\\\\\frac{1}{x+y}\\cdot\\frac{x+y}{xy}&=\\frac{1}{xy}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $x\\ne 0$, $y\\ne 0$ and $x+y\\ne 0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
